


CALL(1C)            UNIX Programmer's Manual             CALL(1C)



NAME
     call - ring a telephone

SYNOPSIS
     call phonenumber

DESCRIPTION
     _C_a_l_l places an outgoing call to the specified _p_h_o_n_e_n_u_m_b_e_r.
     Nothing special happens when the called party answers.
     _P_h_o_n_e_n_u_m_b_e_r may have any number of digits; a `+' sign may be
     used to specify a point at which to wait for a second dial
     tone.

FILES
     /dev/dn0

SEE ALSO
     cu(1), dn(5)





































